---
// SeoContentSection.astro - homepage copy describing only what the site actually does.
---

<section id="about-news-portal" class="w-full py-12 sm:py-16 bg-canvas border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">

    <!-- Section Eyebrow Header -->
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center mb-10">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 bg-gradient-start text-primary-strong font-mono-caption text-[11px] font-bold rounded-full border border-hairline mb-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary animate-pulse"></span>
        NEWS AGGREGATION & VERIFICATION PORTAL
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink tracking-[-1.2px] max-w-3xl">
        Real-Time News & AI Fact Check Portal — NewzWale
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-body mt-2 max-w-2xl">
        Live English-language headlines from Indian news sources, plus a claim-verification tool that checks evidence before it answers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main SEO Grid Content -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 sm:gap-8">

      <!-- Box 1: Live News -->
      <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-surface-card border border-hairline rounded-md shadow-stacked-sm hover:border-primary transition-colors space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-md bg-primary-strong text-on-primary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg shadow-stacked-sm">
          📰
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
          Breaking News Today & Live India News Coverage
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          Welcome to <strong>NewzWale</strong>, a digital hub for <strong>latest news</strong>, <strong>breaking news</strong>, and <strong>india news</strong>, pulled straight from source feeds rather than rewritten by hand.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          Headlines are fetched live from NewsData.io for India, with an RSS fallback across The Hindu, The Indian Express, NDTV, and Mint whenever the primary feed comes back empty. Every card links straight through to the original publisher, tagged with its source and category, newest first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Box 2: Fact Check Pipeline -->
      <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-surface-card border border-hairline rounded-md shadow-stacked-sm hover:border-primary transition-colors space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-md bg-primary-strong text-on-primary flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg shadow-stacked-sm">
            🔍
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[11px] font-mono-caption text-primary-strong font-bold">VERIFICATION ENGINE</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
              Fact Check Explorer & Fact Check India
            </h3>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          Paste a headline, a claim, or an article URL into the <a href="/fact-check" class="text-primary-strong hover:underline">fact-check tool</a> and it runs a three-stage pipeline: first it checks Google's Fact Check Tools database for an existing review; if nothing certified turns up, it runs a web search, fetches the matching pages, and asks a Workers AI model to weigh the claim against that evidence.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-primary-strong font-bold">✓</span>
            <span>A verdict of Verified, Misleading, or False is only returned when the retrieved evidence actually supports it.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-primary-strong font-bold">✓</span>
            <span>When the evidence is thin, the tool says so — "not enough evidence to judge" — instead of guessing.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-primary-strong font-bold">✓</span>
            <span>Every result links back to the sources it read, so you can check the reasoning yourself.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="pt-6 sm:pt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 text-[11px] font-mono text-mute">
      <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-full">#news</span>
      <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-full">#newstoday</span>
      <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-full">#indianews</span>
      <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-full">#factcheck</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
